    {
      "short": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\">\n          <li><b>Users × actions ÷ 100k s</b> gives average requests per second.</li>\n          <li>Multiply by <b>2–3×</b> for the peak, and size for that.</li>\n          <li><b>Servers</b> = peak ÷ per-server capacity, plus headroom.</li>\n          <li><b>Storage</b> = items/day × size × 365 × copies.</li>\n          <li>Estimate <b>bytes out</b> and <b>memory</b> too — they often decide the design.</li>\n        </ul>"
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "next",
        "text": "That finishes Foundations. Next: <b>Vertical vs Horizontal Scaling</b> — what to do when the numbers say one machine won’t do."
      },
